<section class="aq-section"><div class="aq-in aq-stack-l"><header class="aq-sec-head"><h2 class="aq-h1">From protocol to release, then SAT</h2></header><ol class="aq-rows aq-steps aq-steps--hold"><li><div class="aq-rows__row"><span class="aq-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3 class="aq-rows__t">Draft protocol</h3><p class="aq-rows__d">From the approved functional specification, sent <span class="aq-ph">[protocol issue before FAT, weeks]</span> ahead. Every test case has an acceptance criterion and a URS reference.</p></div></li><li class="is-hold"><div class="aq-rows__row"><span class="aq-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3 class="aq-rows__t">Your review and approval</h3><p class="aq-rows__d">Your validation team comments and may add test cases (Annex 15, 2.6); we answer in writing. Nothing runs before your quality unit signs.</p><span class="aq-steps__gate"><svg class="aq-steps__valve" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 1 L12 15 L4 15 L12 1 Z"></path><path d="M8 8 H15 M15 4 V12"></path></svg></span><span class="aq-steps__hold"><span class="aq-steps__stamp">Hold point</span><span class="aq-steps__who">Signed by your quality unit</span><span class="aq-steps__sign" aria-hidden="true">Sign</span></span></div></li><li><div class="aq-rows__row"><span class="aq-index" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3 class="aq-rows__t">Internal dry run</h3><p class="aq-rows__d">We run the full protocol ourselves first and fix what it finds, so the witnessed FAT confirms the system rather than debugs it.</p></div></li><li><div class="aq-rows__row"><span class="aq-index" aria-hidden="true">04</span><h3 class="aq-rows__t">Witnessed execution</h3><p class="aq-rows__d">On our floor, remote or both. Results recorded as found, raw data attached, fabrication hold points already closed.</p></div></li><li><div class="aq-rows__row"><span class="aq-index" aria-hidden="true">05</span><h3 class="aq-rows__t">Deviations and punch list</h3><p class="aq-rows__d">A failed acceptance criterion is a deviation: investigated, fixed, retested (Annex 15, 2.8). A defect that changes no result goes on the punch list.</p></div></li><li class="is-hold"><div class="aq-rows__row"><span class="aq-index" aria-hidden="true">06</span><h3 class="aq-rows__t">Report and release to ship</h3><p class="aq-rows__d">Signed by both parties. Open deviations ship only on a quality-unit-approved no-impact assessment. Skid drained, then <span class="aq-ph">[post-FAT drying and sealing method]</span>.</p><span class="aq-steps__gate"><svg class="aq-steps__valve" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 1 L12 15 L4 15 L12 1 Z"></path><path d="M8 8 H15 M15 4 V12"></path></svg></span><span class="aq-steps__hold"><span class="aq-steps__stamp">Hold point</span><span class="aq-steps__who">Signed by both parties</span><span class="aq-steps__sign" aria-hidden="true">Sign</span></span></div></li><li><div class="aq-rows__row"><span class="aq-index" aria-hidden="true">07</span><h3 class="aq-rows__t">SAT on your site</h3><p class="aq-rows__d">Critical tests re-run on your feed water, utilities and loop, conductivity read uncompensated (USP &lt;645&gt; stage 1). Then handed to IQ/OQ.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>
</div>
